From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 09:25:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Add a t880 board profile and per-drive root overrides

Alldocube iPlay 80 mini Ultra (T880, MT6897) profile for the launcher:
the same read-only NV partitions as qqcandy, with the modem OTA store
mounted at /mnt/vendor/mdota (as Android on this tablet) from mcf_ota_a,
the slot whose LK loads the modem image under Linux.

MTK_CCCI_DRIVE_ROOTS lets a board integration replace the candidate roots
of individual FS drives without changing the qqcandy defaults, e.g.
"T=/mnt/vendor/mdota:/vendor/etc/mdota". Invalid entries are refused.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 README.md                             |  3 ++-
 src/mtk_ccci_userspace/mdinit.py      | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 src/mtk_ccci_userspace/start_owner.py | 26 +++++++++++++++++++-------
 3 files changed, 39 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 8c3bb4a..6e648f6 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -48,7 +48,8 @@ The owner uses environment variables instead of hard-coded private paths:
 - `MTK_CCCI_VENDOR_ETC_ROOT`
 - `MTK_CCCI_PRIVATE_ROOT`
 - `MTK_CCCI_PROPERTY_TABLE`
-- `MTK_CCCI_BOARD` (currently only `qqcandy`)
+- `MTK_CCCI_BOARD` (`qqcandy` or `t880`)
+- `MTK_CCCI_DRIVE_ROOTS` (optional per-drive root overrides)
 - `MTK_CCCI_EXPECTED_KERNEL`
 - `MTK_CCCI_EXPECTED_NOTES_SHA256`
 - `MTK_CCCI_ENABLE_MDLOG` (disabled by default)
diff --git a/src/mtk_ccci_userspace/mdinit.py b/src/mtk_ccci_userspace/mdinit.py
index db49d5c..94f72b1 100644
--- a/src/mtk_ccci_userspace/mdinit.py
+++ b/src/mtk_ccci_userspace/mdinit.py
@@ -174,6 +174,24 @@ DRIVE_ROOTS = {
 # private-data drive observed directly in run9, not a protected partition.
 DRIVE_ORDER = ("Z", "X", "Y", "W", "V", "U", "T", "S", "R", "Q")
 
+# Board integrations may replace the candidate roots of individual drives:
+# MTK_CCCI_DRIVE_ROOTS="T=/mnt/vendor/mdota:/vendor/etc/mdota;S=/mnt/vendor/nvcfg"
+# (letters from DRIVE_ORDER, absolute paths, tried in order as above).
+def _drive_root_overrides(spec):
+    roots = {}
+    for item in filter(None, (part.strip() for part in spec.split(";"))):
+        letter, _, paths = item.partition("=")
+        letter = letter.strip().upper()
+        candidates = [p for p in paths.split(":") if p]
+        if (letter not in DRIVE_ORDER or not candidates or
+                not all(os.path.isabs(p) for p in candidates)):
+            raise ValueError("invalid MTK_CCCI_DRIVE_ROOTS entry %r" % item)
+        roots[letter] = candidates
+    return roots
+
+
+DRIVE_ROOTS.update(_drive_root_overrides(os.environ.get("MTK_CCCI_DRIVE_ROOTS", "")))
+
 
 def resolve_drive_dirs(roots=None):
     """Bind each official drive letter to the first EXISTING candidate root.
diff --git a/src/mtk_ccci_userspace/start_owner.py b/src/mtk_ccci_userspace/start_owner.py
index 1babdc1..946b54c 100644
--- a/src/mtk_ccci_userspace/start_owner.py
